WEBVTT

00:00:11.239 --> 00:00:13.269
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:13.275 --> 00:00:15.193
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:15.194 --> 00:00:16.513
The family business.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.602
You know the truth about
Sammy and the other children.

00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:24.834
I've known for a while.

00:00:24.848 --> 00:00:26.448
Dad, you know the demon

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:29.294
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:00:29.442 --> 00:00:30.727
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.290
No, I don't.

00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:33.963
Did he say anything to you?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.447
No.

00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:39.174
Nothing.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.794
Max, your abilities started
6,7 months ago, right?

00:00:42.895 --> 00:00:45.154
How'd you know that? 'Cause
that's when my abilities started.

00:00:45.186 --> 00:00:46.099
You and I...

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:47.925
We're chosen. For what?

00:00:48.011 --> 00:00:49.065
I don't know.

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:51.090
Everyone's capable of murder. Everyone.

00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:53.208
You know, maybe that's what
the demon's doing, pushing us,

00:00:53.242 --> 00:00:54.543
Finding ways to break us.

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:55.713
Sam, we don't know what the demon wants.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.147
We all have some kind
of ability. Ability?

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.064
Psychic ability. I have visions,

00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:02.249
Premonitions. It's
different for everybody.

00:01:02.274 --> 00:01:04.904
The demon said he had
plans for people like us.

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:07.307
What kind of plans? We
don't really know for sure.

00:01:10.228 --> 00:01:11.499
Don't be afraid, Scott.

00:01:11.594 --> 00:01:13.116
You can tell me anything. You know that.

00:01:14.309 --> 00:01:16.578
Whatever you say, it
won't leave this room.

00:01:20.069 --> 00:01:22.279
It started a little over a year ago.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.451
Migraines at first.

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:29.833
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:01:30.345 --> 00:01:32.138
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.003
I have this ability.

00:01:36.644 --> 00:01:38.067
When I touch something,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.321
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:01:43.572 --> 00:01:44.882
How do you know?

00:01:47.132 --> 00:01:49.086
Did it to the neighbor's cat.

00:01:51.207 --> 00:01:53.855
Its insides fried up like a hamburger.

00:01:58.602 --> 00:01:59.813
You don't believe me.

00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:04.913
I believe that you believe it.

00:02:07.195 --> 00:02:08.118
Then here.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.423
Want to shake on it?

00:02:22.052 --> 00:02:24.583
Why would you want to kill
the neighbor's cat, Scott?

00:02:24.669 --> 00:02:25.891
I don't.

00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:29.792
He wants me to and he
doesn't want me to stop there.

00:02:29.867 --> 00:02:30.910
Who?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.193
The yellow-Eyed man.

00:02:34.658 --> 00:02:36.558
He comes to me in my dreams.

00:02:37.132 --> 00:02:39.701
He tells me to do things, awful things

00:02:40.298 --> 00:02:42.207
But I tell him no.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.851
"No, I don't want to!"

00:02:45.795 --> 00:02:48.206
What else does the
yellow-Eyed man tell you?

00:02:53.401 --> 00:02:55.124
He has plans for me.

00:02:55.146 --> 00:02:56.770
What kind of plans?

00:02:58.502 --> 00:03:02.637
And you've just had
some kind of mushroom

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.207
And your mind is moving low

00:03:07.214 --> 00:03:10.919
Go ask Alice

00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:14.076
I think she'll know

00:03:16.724 --> 00:03:20.251
When logic and proportion

00:03:20.348 --> 00:03:21.240
Hello?

00:03:21.294 --> 00:03:25.181
Have fallen softly dead

00:03:25.197 --> 00:03:29.863
And the white knight
is talking backwards

00:03:29.927 --> 00:03:34.134
And the red queen's, "off with her head"

00:03:34.907 --> 00:03:37.296
Remember

00:03:37.821 --> 00:03:41.328
What the dormouse said

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.232
Feed your head

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.562
Before dad died, he...

00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:06.649
He told me something.

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:10.142
Something about you.

00:04:11.973 --> 00:04:13.217
What?

00:04:16.964 --> 00:04:18.624
Dean, what did he tell you?

00:04:19.687 --> 00:04:20.642
He said that he...

00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:23.723
Wanted me to watch out for you...

00:04:24.779 --> 00:04:26.260
Take care of you.

00:04:27.212 --> 00:04:29.075
He told you that a million times.

00:04:29.128 --> 00:04:30.440
Well, this time was different.

00:04:31.942 --> 00:04:33.234
He said that I had to...

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:35.978
Save you.

00:04:37.411 --> 00:04:38.754
Save me from what?

00:04:38.848 --> 00:04:40.722
He just said that I had to save you

00:04:40.724 --> 00:04:41.968
And nothing else mattered

00:04:42.044 --> 00:04:44.883
And that if I couldn't, I'd...

00:04:45.817 --> 00:04:47.587
You'd what, Dean?

00:04:49.019 --> 00:04:50.432
I'd have to kill you.

00:04:55.187 --> 00:04:57.697
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sammy.

00:04:58.272 --> 00:04:59.423
Kill me?

00:05:02.192 --> 00:05:04.202
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.061
I don't know.

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.279
He must have had some kinda
reason for saying it, right?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.412
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:05:09.459 --> 00:05:11.439
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:05:12.134 --> 00:05:14.614
What else did he say,
Dean? That's it, I swear.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.799
How could you not have told
me this? Because it was dad,

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.564
And he begged me not to. Who cares!

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:20.918
Take some responsibility
for yourself, Dean!

00:05:21.173 --> 00:05:23.095
You had no right to keep this from me!

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.453
You  think I wanted this?

00:05:24.928 --> 00:05:25.970
Huh?

00:05:26.095 --> 00:05:28.443
I wish to god he'd
never opened his mouth.

00:05:29.109 --> 00:05:32.247
Then I wouldn't have to walk around
with this screaming in my head all day!

00:05:39.577 --> 00:05:41.218
We each got to figure
out what's going on,

00:05:41.224 --> 00:05:42.906
Then, what the hell all this means.

00:05:45.564 --> 00:05:46.630
We do?

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.721
I've been thinking about this.
I think we should just lay low,

00:05:49.768 --> 00:05:51.906
You  know. At least for a while.

00:05:51.952 --> 00:05:53.296
It would be safer.

00:05:54.378 --> 00:05:56.039
That way, I could make sure...

00:05:56.134 --> 00:05:57.128
What?

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.792
That I don't turn evil?

00:05:59.815 --> 00:06:02.435
That I don't turn into
some kind of killer?

00:06:02.441 --> 00:06:04.144
I never said that.
Jeez, you're not careful,

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.858
You will have to waste me one day, Dean.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.098
I never said that!

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:11.231
Damn it, Sam, this whole thing
is spinning out of control.

00:06:11.752 --> 00:06:14.412
All right? You're immune
to some weirdo demon virus

00:06:15.516 --> 00:06:17.527
And I don't even know
what the hell anymore.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.123
And you're pissed at me, and I
get it. That's fine. I deserve it.

00:06:26.003 --> 00:06:28.955
But we lay low until we
figure out our next move, okay?

00:06:29.038 --> 00:06:30.239
Forget it.

00:06:32.202 --> 00:06:34.184
Sam, please, man.

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:35.971
Hey, please.

00:06:37.353 --> 00:06:39.113
Just give me some time.

00:06:39.888 --> 00:06:41.237
Give me some time to think, okay?

00:06:41.273 --> 00:06:43.964
I'm begging you here. Please, please...

00:09:10.276 --> 00:09:11.158
Honey?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.471
Are you okay?

00:09:14.737 --> 00:09:16.239
Oh, I just had another nightmare.

00:09:16.325 --> 00:09:17.744
It's fine. It's nothing.

00:09:17.851 --> 00:09:19.342
Just go back to sleep.

00:09:19.965 --> 00:09:21.139
Sure?

00:09:22.191 --> 00:09:23.993
Yeah. Okay.

00:09:44.129 --> 00:09:45.081
Sam.

00:09:45.304 --> 00:09:46.469
Hey, Ellen.

00:09:49.007 --> 00:09:51.120
You don't seem that surprised to see me.

00:09:51.154 --> 00:09:52.677
Your brother's been
calling, worry to say,

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.164
Looking for you. Yeah.

00:09:54.595 --> 00:09:55.848
I figured he might.

00:09:55.884 --> 00:09:57.655
What's going on between you two?

00:10:00.064 --> 00:10:01.157
So, um...

00:10:02.225 --> 00:10:03.531
How's Jo?

00:10:05.979 --> 00:10:07.585
Well, I don't really know.

00:10:07.631 --> 00:10:10.047
What do you mean? I
haven't seen her in weeks.

00:10:10.128 --> 00:10:11.956
She sends a postcard now and again.

00:10:11.982 --> 00:10:13.244
Well, what happened?

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.969
Well, after she worked
that job with you boys

00:10:16.044 --> 00:10:17.846
She decided she wanted
to keep on hunting.

00:10:18.448 --> 00:10:20.189
I said, "not under my roof,"

00:10:20.195 --> 00:10:22.347
And she said "fine".

00:10:23.919 --> 00:10:27.783
So I'm probably the last person
you want to see right now.

00:10:29.618 --> 00:10:32.147
Oh, don't get me wrong.

00:10:32.232 --> 00:10:35.202
I wish I could blame
the hell out of you boys.

00:10:35.933 --> 00:10:37.186
It would be easier.

00:10:37.252 --> 00:10:40.169
The truth is, it's not your fault.

00:10:40.595 --> 00:10:41.885
Sam,

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.963
None of it is.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:48.422
I want you to know that

00:10:49.038 --> 00:10:51.459
I forgave your daddy a long time ago...

00:10:52.509 --> 00:10:54.320
For what happened to my Bill.

00:10:55.984 --> 00:10:58.463
I just don't think he
ever forgave himself.

00:10:59.488 --> 00:11:01.119
What did happen?

00:11:04.994 --> 00:11:08.056
Um, so, why did you come here, sweetie?

00:11:09.926 --> 00:11:11.249
I need help.

00:11:11.402 --> 00:11:13.065
So, what am I looking for, Sam?

00:11:13.108 --> 00:11:15.009
Other people, other...

00:11:15.454 --> 00:11:17.177
Psychics like me.

00:11:17.281 --> 00:11:20.579
As many as possible and I
need a nationwide search.

00:11:20.633 --> 00:11:21.757
But

00:11:21.761 --> 00:11:24.062
I thought there was no
way to track them all down.

00:11:24.156 --> 00:11:26.487
Not all of them had
nursery fires like you did.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:27.885
Well...

00:11:27.888 --> 00:11:29.862
No, but some had to.

00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:30.948
Start there.

00:11:35.163 --> 00:11:36.000
Done...

00:11:36.003 --> 00:11:37.246
And done.

00:11:37.351 --> 00:11:39.022
That was fast. Well,

00:11:39.058 --> 00:11:40.938
Apparently, that's my job.

00:11:41.023 --> 00:11:43.243
Make the monkey dance. Key boarding.

00:11:43.267 --> 00:11:45.012
Just tell us what you got, Ash.

00:11:45.047 --> 00:11:48.751
Four folks fit the profile nationwide.

00:11:48.808 --> 00:11:51.675
Born in '83, mother
died in a nursery fire,

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:53.723
The whole shebang. Four? That's it?

00:11:53.749 --> 00:11:56.727
Sam Winchester from Lawrence, Kansas.

00:11:56.791 --> 00:11:58.464
Max Miller from Saginaw, Michigan,

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.947
Andrew Gallagher from Guthrie, Oklahoma

00:12:01.842 --> 00:12:02.903
And

00:12:02.918 --> 00:12:04.762
Another name,

00:12:04.767 --> 00:12:05.979
Scott Carey.

00:12:08.037 --> 00:12:09.321
What? You got an address?

00:12:09.347 --> 00:12:10.459
Kind of.

00:12:11.054 --> 00:12:15.938
The arbor hills cemetery
in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:12:16.002 --> 00:12:18.463
Plot 486. So he's dead?

00:12:18.558 --> 00:12:21.359
Killed about a month ago. Killed how?

00:12:21.392 --> 00:12:22.623
Stabbed.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.353
Parking lot.

00:12:25.036 --> 00:12:26.747
Fuzz don't have much.

00:12:27.229 --> 00:12:28.694
No suspects.

00:12:31.823 --> 00:12:32.723
All right.

00:12:33.019 --> 00:12:34.383
Thank you.

00:12:39.237 --> 00:12:41.228
Where are you going? Indiana.

00:12:41.313 --> 00:12:42.285
Sam,

00:12:43.149 --> 00:12:45.251
I got to call Dean. I've got
to let him know where you are.

00:12:45.324 --> 00:12:47.645
Ellen, I'm trying to find answers

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.262
About who I am

00:12:49.766 --> 00:12:53.085
And my brother means well, but
he can't protect me from that.

00:12:54.896 --> 00:12:56.097
Please.

00:13:01.592 --> 00:13:03.601
You said you went to
high school with Scott?

00:13:04.208 --> 00:13:06.098
Uh, yes, sir, I did.

00:13:06.414 --> 00:13:09.293
I just heard about what
happened. I'm so sorry.

00:13:09.707 --> 00:13:11.078
Scotty was a good boy.

00:13:12.172 --> 00:13:14.081
He changed a lot since you knew him.

00:13:14.127 --> 00:13:15.660
What do you mean?

00:13:16.063 --> 00:13:19.462
It started about a year
ago with these headaches.

00:13:19.567 --> 00:13:22.516
Then he got depressed, paranoid.

00:13:22.988 --> 00:13:25.048
Nightmares. Nightmares?

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.019
Did he ever talk to you about
his nightmares, what he saw?

00:13:31.122 --> 00:13:32.144
No, no,

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.113
He  closed up on me.

00:13:34.127 --> 00:13:36.478
I  tried to get him
help, but nothing took.

00:13:37.209 --> 00:13:38.335
He'd just...

00:13:39.136 --> 00:13:41.308
Lock himself in his room for days.

00:13:42.599 --> 00:13:44.629
You think maybe I could see his room?

00:15:04.266 --> 00:15:05.858
Who are you? Please...

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.843
You're in danger.

00:15:08.975 --> 00:15:11.675
Okay, look, I know how all this sounds,

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.409
But I am not insane,
and I'm not on drugs.

00:15:14.516 --> 00:15:16.069
Okay, I am normal,

00:15:16.101 --> 00:15:18.762
And this is way, way off the map for me.

00:15:18.787 --> 00:15:19.910
All right, all right, just...

00:15:20.493 --> 00:15:22.495
Just calm down, okay?

00:15:23.219 --> 00:15:25.098
What's your name? Ava.

00:15:25.144 --> 00:15:26.508
Ava? Ava Wilson.

00:15:26.553 --> 00:15:28.950
Ava, I'm Sam Winchester, all right?

00:15:29.026 --> 00:15:32.603
Now, you were telling me
about these dreams of yours?

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.530
Oh, yeah, uh, okay.

00:15:34.536 --> 00:15:38.085
About a year ago, I started having
these like headaches, and just...

00:15:38.399 --> 00:15:41.216
Nightmares, I guess. And I
really didn't think much of it

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:45.518
Until I had this one dream where I saw
this guy get stabbed in a parking lot.

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:48.283
When was this?

00:15:48.327 --> 00:15:50.996
Uh, about a month ago. But anyway,

00:15:51.041 --> 00:15:52.812
A couple of days later...

00:15:54.376 --> 00:15:55.897
I found this.

00:15:59.474 --> 00:16:01.715
I saw this guy die

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.079
Days before it happened.

00:16:04.105 --> 00:16:07.116
I don't know why. I don't
know. It's just for some reason,

00:16:07.809 --> 00:16:10.490
My dreams are coming true,

00:16:10.505 --> 00:16:11.695
And

00:16:11.702 --> 00:16:13.391
Last night,

00:16:13.399 --> 00:16:15.170
I had another one.

00:16:15.851 --> 00:16:16.956
Okay.

00:16:17.032 --> 00:16:18.462
About you.

00:16:20.465 --> 00:16:22.413
I saw you die.

00:16:26.502 --> 00:16:27.794
How did you find me?

00:16:29.066 --> 00:16:31.725
You had motel stationery,
and I googled the motel,

00:16:31.811 --> 00:16:34.921
And it was real, and so I
just thought that I should

00:16:34.925 --> 00:16:36.365
Warn you.

00:16:38.279 --> 00:16:39.560
I don't believe this.

00:16:41.032 --> 00:16:42.583
Of course you don't.

00:16:42.658 --> 00:16:44.700
You think I'm a total nutjob.

00:16:44.936 --> 00:16:46.526
Wait! No, no, no.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.692
I mean, you must be one of us.

00:16:49.426 --> 00:16:51.996
Sorry, one of... One of who?

00:16:52.181 --> 00:16:54.899
One of the psychics, like me.

00:16:55.412 --> 00:16:56.477
Look, Ava, I have visions too, all
right? So... so we're connected.

00:17:02.978 --> 00:17:05.558
Okay, so... you're nuts.

00:17:05.604 --> 00:17:08.191
That's great. No,
okay, okay. Okay, look.

00:17:08.226 --> 00:17:11.226
Did your mother happen
to die in a house fire?

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.683
No, my mother lives in Palm Beach.

00:17:13.745 --> 00:17:15.687
So you don't fit the pattern either.

00:17:22.688 --> 00:17:23.682
Hello?

00:17:23.727 --> 00:17:24.669
It's Ellen.

00:17:24.703 --> 00:17:26.098
Hey, have you heard from Sam?

00:17:26.202 --> 00:17:27.124
I have.

00:17:27.129 --> 00:17:30.479
But he made me promise not
to tell you where he is.

00:17:30.503 --> 00:17:31.934
Come on, Ellen, please.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.972
Something bad could be
going on here, and I swore

00:17:33.977 --> 00:17:35.330
I'd look after that kid.

00:17:35.384 --> 00:17:38.450
Dean, let's say you can't
protect your loved ones forever.

00:17:40.075 --> 00:17:41.417
Well, I say screw that.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:42.901
What else is family for?

00:17:44.615 --> 00:17:46.457
He's in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.243
Thanks.

00:17:49.673 --> 00:17:51.367
Why can't you just leave town,

00:17:51.372 --> 00:17:53.094
Please, before you blow up?

00:17:54.164 --> 00:17:55.338
No, I can't.

00:17:55.434 --> 00:17:58.103
Oh, god. Why not?

00:17:58.289 --> 00:18:00.528
Because there's something
going on here, Ava,

00:18:01.031 --> 00:18:02.433
With you, with me.

00:18:02.599 --> 00:18:04.650
I mean, there are
others like us out there

00:18:04.735 --> 00:18:07.086
And we're all a part of something,

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.308
And I've got to figure out what.

00:18:09.394 --> 00:18:11.314
Okay, you know what?

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.550
Screw you, buddy. Okay?

00:18:13.586 --> 00:18:16.374
'Cause I'm a secretary from Peoria
and I'm not part of anything.

00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:17.902
Do you see this?

00:18:17.936 --> 00:18:20.157
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:18:20.243 --> 00:18:22.146
I am supposed to be at
home addressing invitations

00:18:22.188 --> 00:18:24.601
Which I am way behind on, by the way.

00:18:24.655 --> 00:18:28.132
But instead, I drove out
here to save your weirdo ass.

00:18:28.219 --> 00:18:31.865
But if you just want to
stay here and die, fine.

00:18:32.098 --> 00:18:33.163
Me?

00:18:33.217 --> 00:18:35.209
I'm due back on planet earth.

00:18:35.293 --> 00:18:37.145
Don't you wanna know
why this is happening?

00:18:38.854 --> 00:18:41.537
I mean, don't these visions
scare the hell out of you?

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:45.409
'Cause if you walk out
that door right now,

00:18:46.721 --> 00:18:48.621
You might never know the truth.

00:18:52.497 --> 00:18:54.032
I need your help.

00:18:54.117 --> 00:18:56.198
So, Miss Wilson, you're new in town?

00:18:56.791 --> 00:18:57.922
That's right.

00:18:57.998 --> 00:19:00.438
And what made you decide
to seek out therapy?

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.611
I have no idea.

00:19:04.006 --> 00:19:04.957
No?

00:19:05.043 --> 00:19:08.173
No, I mean, I'm feeling really, super...

00:19:09.007 --> 00:19:11.415
Anxious right now.

00:19:11.501 --> 00:19:13.472
Okay, anything else?

00:19:16.731 --> 00:19:18.483
Holy crap! What?!

00:19:23.006 --> 00:19:25.576
I just remembered, when I was a kid,

00:19:25.611 --> 00:19:28.351
I swallowed like eight things of pop
rocks, and then drank a whole can of coke.

00:19:28.436 --> 00:19:31.547
You don't think that that counts
as a suicide attempt, do you?

00:19:41.472 --> 00:19:42.884
You okay?

00:19:44.415 --> 00:19:45.616
Am I okay?

00:19:45.663 --> 00:19:46.547
Yeah.

00:19:46.601 --> 00:19:50.247
I just helped you steal some dead
guy's confidential psych files.

00:19:50.451 --> 00:19:51.965
I'm awesome!

00:19:53.415 --> 00:19:55.156
It started a little over a year ago.

00:19:55.643 --> 00:19:57.554
Migraines at first.

00:19:58.696 --> 00:20:01.725
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.150
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:20:03.175 --> 00:20:04.558
I have this ability.

00:20:06.351 --> 00:20:07.943
When I touch something,

00:20:07.946 --> 00:20:10.166
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:20:31.102 --> 00:20:32.733
Oh, thank god you're okay.

00:20:39.782 --> 00:20:41.643
Oh, you're better than okay.

00:20:41.668 --> 00:20:44.178
Sam, you sly dog.

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.120
What else does the yellow-Eyed man say?

00:20:48.645 --> 00:20:51.344
He has plans for me.

00:20:54.296 --> 00:20:56.197
He says there's a war coming,

00:20:56.738 --> 00:20:58.839
And people like me...

00:20:58.847 --> 00:21:00.775
We're gonna be the soldiers.

00:21:01.231 --> 00:21:03.490
Everything is about to change.

00:21:03.887 --> 00:21:06.766
He's not talking about us, right?

00:21:07.469 --> 00:21:09.189
Yeah, I think he is.

00:21:13.777 --> 00:21:17.052
Well... but how can we turn into that?

00:21:20.213 --> 00:21:21.216
I don't...

00:21:22.499 --> 00:21:23.769
Get down! Oh my god!

00:21:24.592 --> 00:21:26.117
Oh, my god, what's happening?

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:40.785
Gordon!

00:21:47.826 --> 00:21:49.301
You do that to my brother,

00:21:49.304 --> 00:21:51.055
I'll kill you! Dean, wait!

00:22:10.151 --> 00:22:12.371
Wait, I don't understand.

00:22:12.479 --> 00:22:14.877
Shouldn't we be talking to the cops?

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:17.932
Trust me, they wouldn't do us much good.

00:22:25.132 --> 00:22:27.941
These are 223 caliber, subsonic rounds.

00:22:28.027 --> 00:22:30.416
The guy must have put a
suppressor on the rifle.

00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:34.448
Dude, who are you?!

00:22:35.044 --> 00:22:37.311
Oh, I just, uh

00:22:37.827 --> 00:22:40.066
I just watch a lot of "T.J.Hooker".

00:22:45.071 --> 00:22:46.166
Who you calling?

00:22:46.201 --> 00:22:47.114
My brother.

00:22:47.207 --> 00:22:49.068
I think we definitely need help.

00:22:50.072 --> 00:22:51.054
Hello?

00:22:51.069 --> 00:22:53.140
Dean. Sam, I've been looking for you.

00:22:53.545 --> 00:22:55.728
Yeah, look, I'm in Indiana.

00:22:55.759 --> 00:22:57.882
Lafayette. I know.

00:22:57.985 --> 00:22:58.930
You do?

00:22:59.675 --> 00:23:01.204
Yeah, I talked to Ellen.

00:23:01.248 --> 00:23:03.003
I just got here myself.

00:23:03.336 --> 00:23:05.089
It's a real funky town.

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:07.451
You ditched me, Sammy.

00:23:07.546 --> 00:23:10.834
Yeah, I'm sorry. Look, right now,

00:23:10.921 --> 00:23:12.763
There's someone after me. What? Who?

00:23:12.825 --> 00:23:14.898
I don't know. That's
what we need to find out.

00:23:15.623 --> 00:23:16.924
Where are you?

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:20.826
I'm staying at 5637 Monroe
street. Why don't you meet me here?

00:23:20.881 --> 00:23:21.894
Yeah,  sure.

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:27.294
Now, was that so hard?

00:23:27.957 --> 00:23:29.269
Bite me.

00:23:30.809 --> 00:23:31.943
What is it?

00:23:31.957 --> 00:23:33.360
My brother's in trouble.

00:23:33.514 --> 00:23:34.258
What?

00:23:34.923 --> 00:23:36.606
He gave me a code word.

00:23:37.009 --> 00:23:38.599
Someone's got a gun on him.

00:23:39.225 --> 00:23:41.215
Code word? Yeah.

00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:42.583
"Funky town"

00:23:44.282 --> 00:23:46.283
Well, he thought of it.

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:47.254
It's kind of a

00:23:47.266 --> 00:23:48.439
Long story.

00:23:48.983 --> 00:23:49.946
Come on.

00:23:51.599 --> 00:23:52.534
Gordy,

00:23:52.539 --> 00:23:55.598
I know me and Sam ain't exactly
your favorite people, but,

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:57.932
Don't you think this
is a little extreme?

00:23:58.427 --> 00:24:00.447
Oh, you think this is revenge?

00:24:01.268 --> 00:24:03.959
We did leave you tied up in
your own mess for three days.

00:24:04.064 --> 00:24:05.455
Which was awesome.

00:24:06.208 --> 00:24:08.189
Sorry, I shouldn't laugh. Yeah,

00:24:09.152 --> 00:24:11.805
I was definitely planning on
whupping your ass for that.

00:24:12.377 --> 00:24:15.126
That's not what this
is. This isn't personal.

00:24:16.389 --> 00:24:19.139
I'm not a killer, Dean.

00:24:19.581 --> 00:24:20.836
I'm a hunter.

00:24:21.818 --> 00:24:23.951
And your brother is fair game.

00:24:27.908 --> 00:24:29.397
I don't think I should leave.

00:24:29.455 --> 00:24:31.483
I want you out of harm's way, Ava.

00:24:31.977 --> 00:24:33.312
What about you?

00:24:33.406 --> 00:24:35.116
Harm's way doesn't really bother me.

00:24:35.131 --> 00:24:36.034
No, but,

00:24:36.041 --> 00:24:38.149
You are walking right into my vision.

00:24:38.165 --> 00:24:39.699
I mean, this is how you die!

00:24:39.731 --> 00:24:41.144
It doesn't matter.

00:24:42.685 --> 00:24:44.150
It's my brother.

00:24:44.483 --> 00:24:46.033
Maybe I can help.

00:24:46.089 --> 00:24:47.730
You've done all you can. Just...

00:24:48.257 --> 00:24:49.937
Just go back to your fianc.

00:24:51.230 --> 00:24:52.311
Are you sure?

00:24:53.336 --> 00:24:54.987
Yes, I'm sure.

00:24:55.280 --> 00:24:56.643
Go home, Ava.

00:24:56.710 --> 00:24:58.101
You'll be safe there.

00:25:02.745 --> 00:25:03.809
Well, just...

00:25:05.819 --> 00:25:07.364
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:25:07.376 --> 00:25:10.515
When you get your brother, just let
me know that everything's all right.

00:25:11.278 --> 00:25:12.543
I promise.

00:25:13.844 --> 00:25:16.952
See, I was doing an
exorcism down in Louisiana.

00:25:17.376 --> 00:25:20.086
A teenage girl. It seemed routine.

00:25:20.171 --> 00:25:21.804
Some low-Level demon.

00:25:21.867 --> 00:25:24.238
But between all the jabbering
and the head-Spinning,

00:25:24.283 --> 00:25:27.542
The damn thing muttered
something about a coming war.

00:25:27.577 --> 00:25:29.968
I don't think it meant to.
It just kind of slipped out.

00:25:30.002 --> 00:25:31.204
But it was too late.

00:25:31.250 --> 00:25:32.959
It piqued my interest.

00:25:33.007 --> 00:25:36.482
And you can really make a demon
talk when you got the right tools.

00:25:36.548 --> 00:25:38.801
What happened to the
girl it was possessing?

00:25:38.855 --> 00:25:40.308
She didn't make it.

00:25:41.869 --> 00:25:43.731
Well, you're a son of a bitch.

00:25:49.662 --> 00:25:51.683
That's my mama you're talking about.

00:25:53.227 --> 00:25:54.339
Anyway,

00:25:55.499 --> 00:25:59.527
This demon tells me they have
soldiers to fight in this coming war.

00:25:59.543 --> 00:26:02.171
Humans fighting on hell's
side. You believe that?

00:26:02.576 --> 00:26:06.574
I mean, they're psychics, so they're
not exactly pure humans. But still,

00:26:06.607 --> 00:26:10.594
What kind of worthless scumbag you got
to be to turn against your own race?

00:26:12.565 --> 00:26:14.497
But you know the
biggest kick in the ass?

00:26:15.013 --> 00:26:17.244
This demon said I knew one of them

00:26:18.086 --> 00:26:20.777
Our very own Sammy Winchester.

00:26:24.114 --> 00:26:25.148
Well, this is...

00:26:25.230 --> 00:26:27.313
This is a whole new level of moronic,

00:26:27.406 --> 00:26:29.159
Even for you. Yeah?

00:26:30.283 --> 00:26:31.622
Come on, Dean.

00:26:31.627 --> 00:26:32.972
I know

00:26:32.976 --> 00:26:35.038
About Sam's visions.

00:26:36.529 --> 00:26:38.529
I know everything. Really?

00:26:38.923 --> 00:26:40.793
Because a demon told you?

00:26:40.958 --> 00:26:43.359
Yeah, and it wasn't lying. Hey, Dean,

00:26:43.832 --> 00:26:47.104
I'm not some reckless yahoo,
okay? I did my homework.

00:26:47.206 --> 00:26:48.928
I made damn sure it was true.

00:26:49.592 --> 00:26:52.451
Look, you got your
Roadhouse connections.

00:26:52.884 --> 00:26:54.168
I got mine.

00:26:54.574 --> 00:26:57.113
It's how I found Sammy
in the first place.

00:27:05.013 --> 00:27:08.528
About a month ago, I found another
one of these freaks here in town.

00:27:08.566 --> 00:27:11.115
He could deep-Fry a person
just by touching them.

00:27:11.148 --> 00:27:12.581
Yeah, did he kill anyone?

00:27:12.675 --> 00:27:15.254
Besides mr. Tinkles, the cat, no.

00:27:15.320 --> 00:27:17.024
But he was working up to it.

00:27:17.984 --> 00:27:19.816
They're all gonna be killers, Dean.

00:27:19.842 --> 00:27:21.374
We got to take them all out,

00:27:21.380 --> 00:27:23.498
And that means Sammy too.

00:27:28.443 --> 00:27:30.754
You think Sam's stupid enough
to walk through that front door?

00:27:30.828 --> 00:27:32.532
No, I don't.

00:27:32.905 --> 00:27:35.594
Especially since I'm sure
you found a way to warn him.

00:27:37.987 --> 00:27:40.136
You really think I'm that stupid?

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:47.133
No,

00:27:48.026 --> 00:27:50.547
Sammy's gonna scope the place first,

00:27:51.399 --> 00:27:53.549
See me covering the front door.

00:27:54.943 --> 00:27:56.983
So he's gonna take the back.

00:27:57.975 --> 00:28:00.394
And when he does,
he'll hit the tripwire.

00:28:01.977 --> 00:28:03.190
Then...

00:28:08.086 --> 00:28:09.308
Boom.

00:28:10.510 --> 00:28:13.199
Sam's not gonna fall
for a frickin' tripwire.

00:28:14.384 --> 00:28:15.774
Maybe you're right.

00:28:18.875 --> 00:28:20.795
That's why I'll have a second one.

00:28:26.618 --> 00:28:27.800
Hey, look,

00:28:28.843 --> 00:28:30.176
I'm sorry.

00:28:30.950 --> 00:28:33.500
I wish I didn't have
to do this. I really do.

00:28:34.621 --> 00:28:36.244
But for what it's worth,

00:28:37.365 --> 00:28:39.000
It will be quick.

00:29:11.259 --> 00:29:12.403
Come on, man.

00:29:13.125 --> 00:29:15.656
I know Sam, okay? Better than anyone.

00:29:16.128 --> 00:29:18.048
He's got more of a
conscience than I do. I mean,

00:29:18.086 --> 00:29:20.044
The guy feels guilty surfing
the internet for porn.

00:29:20.079 --> 00:29:21.063
Maybe you're right,

00:29:21.728 --> 00:29:23.729
But one day, he's gonna be a monster.

00:29:23.763 --> 00:29:24.527
How?

00:29:25.030 --> 00:29:27.271
Huh? How's a guy like
Sam become a monster?

00:29:27.296 --> 00:29:30.014
It beats me, but he will.
No, you don't know that!

00:29:31.648 --> 00:29:33.228
I'm surprised at you, Dean.

00:29:33.815 --> 00:29:35.384
Getting all emotional.

00:29:36.398 --> 00:29:39.318
I had heard you were more
of a professional than this.

00:29:42.228 --> 00:29:43.150
Look,

00:29:43.163 --> 00:29:47.231
Let's say you're cruising
around in that car of yours.

00:29:47.265 --> 00:29:48.458
And uh,

00:29:48.664 --> 00:29:52.181
You have little Hitler
riding shotgun, right?

00:29:52.705 --> 00:29:54.146
Back when he was just some

00:29:54.152 --> 00:29:56.601
Goofy, crappy artist.

00:29:57.188 --> 00:30:00.585
But you knew what he was
gonna turn into someday.

00:30:01.489 --> 00:30:02.981
You'd take him out.

00:30:03.363 --> 00:30:05.157
No questions, am I right?

00:30:05.201 --> 00:30:06.943
That's not Sam. Yes, it is.

00:30:07.725 --> 00:30:09.516
You just can't see it yet.

00:30:12.118 --> 00:30:14.667
Dean, it's his destiny.

00:30:17.684 --> 00:30:18.758
Look,

00:30:18.762 --> 00:30:20.676
I'm sympathetic.

00:30:21.130 --> 00:30:22.978
He's your brother. You love the guy.

00:30:23.662 --> 00:30:26.103
This has got to hurt like hell for you.

00:30:31.637 --> 00:30:33.319
But here's the thing.

00:30:35.890 --> 00:30:37.391
It would have wrecked him,

00:30:38.504 --> 00:30:39.708
But your dad

00:30:41.130 --> 00:30:42.909
If it really came right down to it,

00:30:42.953 --> 00:30:45.604
He would have had the stones
to do the right thing here.

00:30:46.637 --> 00:30:48.238
So, you're telling me

00:30:49.092 --> 00:30:51.042
You're not the man he is?

00:32:08.593 --> 00:32:09.935
You hear him?

00:32:23.614 --> 00:32:25.077
Here he comes.

00:32:31.546 --> 00:32:32.691
Hold on.

00:32:33.104 --> 00:32:34.538
Not yet.

00:32:35.340 --> 00:32:37.021
Let's wait and see.

00:33:00.428 --> 00:33:01.752
Sorry, Dean.

00:33:26.309 --> 00:33:27.701
Drop the gun.

00:33:29.002 --> 00:33:31.261
You shouldn't take your
shoes off around here.

00:33:31.608 --> 00:33:34.167
You might get tetanus. Put it down now!

00:33:41.597 --> 00:33:43.208
You wouldn't shoot me, would you, Sammy?

00:33:43.980 --> 00:33:46.891
'Cause your brother, he thinks
you're some kind of saint.

00:33:47.295 --> 00:33:48.488
Yeah.

00:33:48.582 --> 00:33:49.784
Well, I wouldn't be so sure.

00:33:50.708 --> 00:33:52.468
See, that's what I said.

00:34:16.867 --> 00:34:19.784
You're no better than the
filthy things you hunt.

00:34:37.655 --> 00:34:38.758
Do it.

00:34:39.582 --> 00:34:40.794
Do it!

00:34:41.278 --> 00:34:43.857
Show your brother the
killer you really are, Sammy.

00:34:52.197 --> 00:34:53.668
It's Sam.

00:35:25.538 --> 00:35:28.448
Son of a bitch... Dean, no.

00:35:28.891 --> 00:35:31.342
I let him live once. I'm not
making the same mistake twice.

00:35:31.438 --> 00:35:32.428
Trust me.

00:35:33.055 --> 00:35:34.865
Gordon's taken care of.

00:35:36.476 --> 00:35:37.488
Come on.

00:36:00.218 --> 00:36:01.841
You call this taken care of?

00:36:06.487 --> 00:36:07.690
What the hell are we doing?

00:36:07.752 --> 00:36:09.367
Just trust me on this. All right?

00:36:17.245 --> 00:36:19.575
Drop your weapons!
Get down on your knees!

00:36:19.611 --> 00:36:20.944
Do it now!

00:36:31.406 --> 00:36:32.939
Put your hands on your head.

00:36:34.013 --> 00:36:35.502
Easy now.

00:36:54.340 --> 00:36:56.042
Anonymous tip.

00:36:56.804 --> 00:36:59.417
You're a fine, upstanding citizen, Sam.

00:37:11.857 --> 00:37:13.498
Gordon Walker was hunting Sam?

00:37:13.512 --> 00:37:14.866
And he almost killed us both 'cause

00:37:14.898 --> 00:37:16.872
Somebody over there can't
keep their frickin' mouth shut.

00:37:17.276 --> 00:37:19.216
And you honestly think that it was me?

00:37:19.711 --> 00:37:20.603
Or Ash or Jo?

00:37:20.607 --> 00:37:21.492
No way.

00:37:21.527 --> 00:37:23.048
Who else knows about Sam, huh?

00:37:24.249 --> 00:37:26.062
Well, you must have
been talking to somebody.

00:37:26.115 --> 00:37:28.197
You can say a lot of things about us

00:37:28.274 --> 00:37:29.525
But we aren't disloyal,

00:37:29.530 --> 00:37:30.882
And we're not stupid.

00:37:30.918 --> 00:37:32.590
We haven't breathed a word of this.

00:37:32.654 --> 00:37:34.666
Gordon said he had
Roadhouse connections, Ellen.

00:37:34.679 --> 00:37:37.461
And this Roadhouse is
full of other hunters.

00:37:39.030 --> 00:37:41.879
They're all smart.
They're good trackers,

00:37:41.925 --> 00:37:44.834
Each of them with their own
patterns and connections.

00:37:44.890 --> 00:37:47.209
Hell, I could name 12 of them right now

00:37:47.216 --> 00:37:49.296
That are capable of
putting this together.

00:37:51.525 --> 00:37:53.858
I am sorry about what happened, Dean,

00:37:54.718 --> 00:37:56.700
But I can't control these people

00:37:56.706 --> 00:37:58.857
Or what they choose to believe.

00:38:05.157 --> 00:38:07.321
Hey, Ava, it's Sam... again.

00:38:08.203 --> 00:38:09.334
Call me when you get this.

00:38:09.439 --> 00:38:11.601
Just want to make
sure you got home okay.

00:38:12.133 --> 00:38:13.688
All right, bye.

00:38:13.702 --> 00:38:15.312
Everything all right?

00:38:16.095 --> 00:38:18.179
Yeah, I hope so.

00:38:18.212 --> 00:38:21.342
Well, Gordon should be reaching for the
soap for the next few years, at least.

00:38:21.426 --> 00:38:22.331
Yeah,

00:38:22.694 --> 00:38:25.193
If they pin Scott
Carey's murder on him...

00:38:25.679 --> 00:38:27.410
And if he doesn't bust out.

00:38:29.997 --> 00:38:32.308
Dude, you ever take
off like that again...

00:38:34.182 --> 00:38:35.312
What?

00:38:35.497 --> 00:38:36.948
You'd kill me?

00:38:38.101 --> 00:38:39.736
That's so not funny.

00:38:40.778 --> 00:38:41.749
All right.

00:38:42.454 --> 00:38:44.716
All right. So, where to next then?

00:38:44.748 --> 00:38:45.782
One word,

00:38:46.267 --> 00:38:48.196
Amsterdam. Dean...

00:38:48.242 --> 00:38:50.882
Come on, man, I hear the coffee
shops don't even serve coffee.

00:38:50.986 --> 00:38:53.317
I'm not gonna just ditch
the job. Screw the job.

00:38:53.862 --> 00:38:56.000
Screw it, man. I'm
sick of the job anyway.

00:38:56.057 --> 00:38:57.111
We don't get paid.

00:38:57.145 --> 00:38:58.247
We don't get thanked.

00:38:58.332 --> 00:38:59.814
The only thing we get is bad luck.

00:39:00.497 --> 00:39:02.258
Well, come on dude, you're a hunter.

00:39:02.363 --> 00:39:04.625
I mean, it's what you were meant to
do. I wasn't meant to do anything.

00:39:04.661 --> 00:39:06.429
I don't believe in that destiny crap.

00:39:06.507 --> 00:39:08.576
You mean you don't
believe in my destiny.

00:39:09.850 --> 00:39:11.020
Whatever.

00:39:12.193 --> 00:39:14.005
Look, Dean, I've tried running before.

00:39:14.438 --> 00:39:16.999
I mean, I ran all the way to
California, and look what happened.

00:39:17.765 --> 00:39:19.324
You can't run from this,

00:39:19.331 --> 00:39:21.002
And you can't protect me.

00:39:23.533 --> 00:39:24.854
I can try.

00:39:27.522 --> 00:39:28.924
Thanks for that.

00:39:33.362 --> 00:39:35.434
Look, Dean, I'm gonna keep hunting.

00:39:36.355 --> 00:39:37.639
I mean, whatever's coming,

00:39:38.261 --> 00:39:41.379
I'm taking it head on so if
you really want to watch my back

00:39:42.016 --> 00:39:43.784
Then I guess you're gonna
have to stick around.

00:39:44.509 --> 00:39:46.351
Bitch. Jerk.

00:39:52.982 --> 00:39:54.443
You calling that Ava girl again?

00:39:54.471 --> 00:39:56.050
You sweet on her or something?

00:39:57.394 --> 00:39:59.105
She's engaged, Dean.

00:39:59.150 --> 00:40:00.183
So?

00:40:00.767 --> 00:40:01.978
What's the point in saving the world,

00:40:01.984 --> 00:40:04.056
If you can't get a little
nookie once in a while, huh?

00:40:07.054 --> 00:40:08.288
What?

00:40:09.288 --> 00:40:10.663
Just a feeling.

00:40:12.921 --> 00:40:15.133
How far is it to Peoria?

00:40:24.980 --> 00:40:25.852
Hello?

00:40:28.960 --> 00:40:30.521
Is anybody home?

00:40:42.432 --> 00:40:43.736
My god...

00:41:00.565 --> 00:41:01.591
Hey.

00:41:04.997 --> 00:41:06.421
Sulfur.

00:41:09.979 --> 00:41:11.480
The demon's been here.

00:41:32.823 --> 00:41:34.215
Ava...

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:12.716
